const source = "# Terms of Service\n\nThis is an English translation of the Japanese Terms of Service. If the English and Japanese versions differ, the Japanese version prevails.\n\n## Article 1 (Application)\n\n1. These Terms of Service (the \"Terms\") set out the conditions for using the services provided by RIZEL (リゼル in Japanese; the \"Operator\").\n2. They cover Tech Phase Research (the \"Service\") and RESOLUTE (the \"Product\"). Users use them after agreeing to these Terms. When applying for the PRO plan or buying the Product, you will be able to read the full text of these Terms and will be asked to confirm that you agree to them.\n3. Articles 18 to 22 apply only to RESOLUTE. All other articles apply to both.\n\n## Article 2 (What the Service Is)\n\n1. The Service organizes and provides information such as news, earnings and stock prices about U.S. technology and semiconductor stocks.\n2. The Service and the Product are intended to provide information for reference in your investment decisions and to help you manage rules you set for yourself. They do not advise on or recommend buying or selling any particular security, continuing to hold it, the timing of trades, or any other investment decision. The Operator is not registered for investment advisory and agency business under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act, and therefore does not answer questions or requests for advice about buying or selling individual securities.\n3. Under the Service and the Product, the Operator never holds your assets and never trades on your behalf.\n\n## Article 3 (Plans)\n\n1. The Service has a FREE plan and a PRO plan.\n2. The PRO plan costs JPY 2,980 per month (tax included) or JPY 29,800 per year (tax included). For users outside Japan, it costs USD 20 per month or USD 200 per year.\n3. The features available on each plan are shown in the Service. The Operator may change features or prices in accordance with Article 16. If the PRO plan price goes up, the Operator will give notice at least 30 days before the change takes effect, and the new price applies from the first renewal date on or after that date.\n\n## Article 4 (Accounts)\n\n1. You must register accurate information and manage your sign-in details on your own responsibility.\n2. Accounts may not be lent, borrowed or transferred.\n3. The Operator is not liable for damage caused by unauthorized use of an account, except where the Operator acted intentionally or negligently.\n4. Minors must obtain the consent of a parent or other legal representative before applying for the PRO plan or buying the Product.\n\n## Article 5 (PRO Plan Fees and Payment)\n\n1. PRO plan fees are paid through PayPal (credit card or bank account). Monthly plans are charged automatically every month, and yearly plans every year.\n2. The billing date is based on the date you applied.\n3. If a payment fails, the Operator may suspend PRO features.\n4. Card details are managed by PayPal; the Operator never receives your card number.\n\n## Article 6 (Cancellation)\n\n1. You can cancel the PRO plan from your account page at any time.\n2. Cancelling does not result in a pro-rated refund of charges already made. You can use the plan until the end of the period you have paid for. However, if you were charged twice or otherwise charged because of an error on the Operator's side, the Operator will refund that amount, and if you could not use the PRO plan for a considerable period for reasons attributable to the Operator, the Operator will refund the fee for that period.\n\n## Article 7 (Notes on Investing)\n\n1. Use the information in the Service and the Product at your own judgment. The Operator is not liable for the results of investments made using that information, except where the Operator acted intentionally or negligently.\n2. Text written or shown by the Operator, such as \"RIZEL's Notes\" and \"RIZEL's Take\", explains facts and information about markets and companies and general attitudes toward investing. It does not advise on or recommend buying or selling any particular security, continuing to hold it, or the timing of trades.\n3. The Operator may hold securities covered in the Service.\n4. Securities such as stocks can lose value because of price movements, exchange-rate movements and other factors, and you may lose part of your principal.\n\n## Article 8 (Accuracy and Delays)\n\n1. Information is based on external data providers and public documents. Its accuracy, completeness and timeliness are not guaranteed.\n2. News on the FREE plan is shown 30 minutes later than on PRO. Delays and gaps can also occur for system reasons.\n3. Some English articles are translated by AI. The accuracy of translations is not guaranteed.\n4. Explanations in \"Earnings deep dive\" describe the content of earnings results; they do not indicate whether to buy or sell.\n\n## Article 9 (Notifications)\n\nNotifications such as browser notifications and phone notifications may not arrive, or may arrive late, depending on your device and connection. The Operator is not liable for damage caused by a notification not arriving or arriving late, except where the Operator acted intentionally or negligently.\n\n## Article 10 (Holdings Display)\n\n1. The holdings you enter are stored on your device.\n2. Information may be lost if your device fails or your browser data is deleted.\n3. Profit, loss and valuation figures shown are for reference and may differ from your broker's records.\n\n## Article 11 (Prohibited Conduct)\n\nYou must not do any of the following.\n\n- Anything that violates laws, public order or good morals\n- Anything that disrupts the operation of the Service or the Product (including excessive access and unauthorized access)\n- Automatically collecting, reposting, reselling or redistributing the content of the Service or the Product\n- Sharing PRO-only content or content for buyers of the Product with third parties\n- Using the information in this service to give others investment advice or solicit investments\n- Anything else the Operator reasonably judges to be inappropriate\n\n## Article 12 (Suspension of Use)\n\nIf you breach the previous article, the Operator may suspend or delete your account without prior notice. Fees in that case are handled under Article 6 for the PRO plan and under Article 22 for the Product.\n\n## Article 13 (Intellectual Property)\n\nRights in the text, design and programs of the Service and the Product belong to the Operator or the rightful owners. External news and data belong to their respective providers. You may use them only for your own personal viewing.\n\n## Article 14 (Changes to and Suspension of the Service)\n\nThe Operator may change, temporarily suspend or end all or part of the Service or the Product for maintenance, changes of data provider and similar reasons. The Operator will announce an ending in advance. The end date will match the end of the last period paid for, and no further charges will be made. Features of the Product without a set period of use can be used until the Operator stops providing the Product. If the Operator stops providing the Product, it will give notice at least three months before the end date.\n\n## Article 15 (Disclaimer)\n\n1. The Operator is not liable for damage arising from use of the Service or the Product, except where the Operator acted intentionally or negligently.\n2. Where the Operator is liable for damages (except where the Operator acted intentionally or with gross negligence), the amount is limited, for the Product, to the fee received for the purchase or the most recent renewal, and for the PRO plan, to one month's fee immediately before the day the cause of the damage occurred (for a yearly plan, one twelfth of the yearly fee). If that amount is less than JPY 3,000 (including on the FREE plan), the limit is JPY 3,000. This paragraph does not limit refunds under Article 6, Paragraph 2 and Article 22, Paragraph 2.\n\n## Article 16 (Changes to These Terms)\n\nThe Operator may change these Terms without your individual consent where the change is in the general interest of users, or where the change does not go against the purpose of the contract and is reasonable in light of the need for the change, the appropriateness of the new content and other circumstances. In that case, the Operator will show the changed Terms and their effective date in the Service a reasonable time before they take effect (at least 30 days for changes that are disadvantageous to users), and will make them known by notice to your registered email address or another appropriate method.\n\n## Article 17 (Governing Law and Jurisdiction)\n\nThese Terms are governed by Japanese law. The Tokyo District Court has exclusive jurisdiction as the court of first instance for disputes.\nThe Japanese version of these Terms is the original, and if the English version differs from it, the Japanese version prevails.\n\n## Article 18 (What the Product Is)\n\n1. The Product is a tool that helps you set your own investing rules and return to them when markets are rough or keep rising. It includes the diagnosis, the market gauge, alerts, the Shock Gauge, the rule charm, a moment to breathe tonight, the tax estimate and My Book.\n2. \"Your investing rules\" shown as the result of the diagnosis are a guide based on your answers and a calculation method the Operator set in advance, and you can change them freely. They do not recommend buying or selling any particular security or the timing of trades.\n3. The tax estimate is provided in the Japanese version only. It shows general calculation examples and is not tax advice. Check actual filing and payment with a tax accountant or tax office.\n4. FREE members of Tech Phase can also buy the Product. Buying the Product is separate from joining the PRO plan.\n\n## Article 19 (Price and Purchase)\n\n1. The Product costs JPY 9,800 (tax included) from March 1, 2027. Until the end of February 2027, it is sold at the launch price of JPY 7,980 (tax included).\n2. A purchase is completed when payment is completed.\n3. You can pay with PayPal (credit card or bank account).\n4. You can start using the Product within 2 days after payment is completed.\n5. The English version is sold in U.S. dollars, at the prices shown on the English pages.\n\n## Article 20 (Gauge and Notifications)\n\n1. The gauge measures (TP Large Cap 100, TP Semiconductor 40 and the TP Fear Index) are reference values the Operator calculates on its own from stock prices supplied by external data providers. They do not match other indices or figures shown by brokers, and they are not related to any index provider. An outline of how they are calculated is shown in the Product.\n2. The Operator may change the constituents and calculation methods of the measures. TP Semiconductor 40's constituents are reviewed four times a year.\n3. Alerts and the Shock Gauge may be late or may not arrive because of your device, connection or data delays.\n4. The Shock Gauge's stars are a guide calculated from the actual index moves after the news and from the article's content, weighing whether the cause looks one-off; they do not indicate future price moves or when to buy or sell. AI may be used to summarize news, and summaries may contain errors.\n5. The Operator is liable for investment results based on these measures and guides, and for damage caused by late or undelivered notifications, as set out in Article 15.\n\n## Article 21 (Period of Use and Renewal of Notifications)\n\n1. The next-morning note, the Shock Gauge, RIZEL's Take and alerts (including closing-price alerts) (the \"Notification Features\") can be used for one year from the date of purchase.\n2. From the second year, you can keep using the Notification Features by renewing. Renewal costs JPY 5,980 (tax included). If you are a Tech Phase PRO member when you pay the renewal fee, it costs JPY 3,980 (tax included).\n3. At least 30 days before the end of the period, the Operator will notify your registered email address of when to renew and the renewal fee.\n4. At your first purchase, with your consent, the Operator saves the PayPal you paid with and renews the Notification Features automatically every year. The renewal fee is paid on the renewal date with the saved PayPal. If you are a Tech Phase PRO member on the renewal date, the PRO member fee applies.\n5. You can stop automatic renewal from your account page until the day before the renewal date. If you stop it, you are not charged the next renewal fee. After you stop it, you can keep using the Notification Features until the end of the period.\n6. If the automatic payment fails, the Operator retries it until 3 days after the renewal date. If it still fails, or if no PayPal is saved, there is no automatic renewal; when you complete the renewal procedure and pay the renewal fee, the period in which you can use the Notification Features is extended by one year. If you do not renew, the Notification Features end at the end of the period.\n7. Even after the Notification Features end, you can keep using the rest of the Product. The parts of the Product other than the Notification Features are a one-time purchase and can be used without a set period, except in the case of Article 14.\n\n## Article 22 (Refunds)\n\n1. Because of the nature of digital products, purchases and renewals are not refunded for reasons of your own convenience.\n2. In the following cases, the Operator will return all or part of the fee received.\n\n(1) When you were charged twice or otherwise charged because of an error on the Operator's side (the amount charged in error)\n\n(2) When, for reasons attributable to the Operator, you could not use all or the main features of the Product for a considerable period (an amount according to the features and period you could not use)\n\n3. This article does not restrict any rights users have under law.\n";
